From: Termux Launcher <noreply@pathayam.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] ldso: read MUSL_LD_PRELOAD instead of LD_PRELOAD

Termux sets LD_PRELOAD to a Bionic library (termux-exec) in every process. A
musl-linked program cannot load it and dies at startup; unsetting the variable
instead removes termux-exec from every child the program spawns, so shebang
scripts break there. Reading a differently named variable leaves LD_PRELOAD
untouched for children and lets the musl process itself ignore it.

--- a/ldso/dynlink.c
+++ b/ldso/dynlink.c
@@ -1822,7 +1822,7 @@ void __dls3(size_t *sp, size_t *auxv)
 	 * and the dynamic linker may need to be loaded itself. */
 	if (!libc.secure) {
 		env_path = getenv("LD_LIBRARY_PATH");
-		env_preload = getenv("LD_PRELOAD");
+		env_preload = getenv("MUSL_LD_PRELOAD");
 	}
 
 	/* If the main program was already loaded by the kernel,
